On 09/22/2013 02:48 AM, oolve...@gmail.com wrote:
> hello. quick question. how can i force lavaan to keep my variables in
> the order in which i entered them? is it possible? for example:

The order of the variables is based on the way you have specified your
model. The lavaan approach is to ignore the data as long as possible: we
parse your model syntax, figure out what is observed and what is latent,
and construct a parameter table. Only when we proceed with fitting the
model, we compute the needed sample statistics based on the data.

You can 'see' the parameter table by typing

parTable(fit)

The 'order' of the observed variables is determined by the output of

lavNames( parTable(fit), type="ov" )

BTW, the equivalent of

>>fitted.values(fit)$cov

for the sample data is

inspect(fit, "sampstat")

which will use the same order as fitted().

Yves.

