Indeed.

it seems like it prints first
> the endogenous/dependent variables, followed by the indpendent/exogenous
> ones in the order where they were specified in the structural equations.

The order is the following:

ov.ind
ov.y
ov.x
other

where ov.ind are observed indicators, ov.y are dependent variables (but
not indicators), ov.x are exogenous variables, and other are everything
not included in the {ov.in <http://ov.in>, ov.y, ov.x}.

> just being curious here. i'm going to be using lavaan to teach some
> basic path analysis/sem and i was hoping that my students could compare
> their model-implied covariance matrices with their observed covariance
> matrices without needing to re-ordering them first so they match each
> other exactly.

You will need to reorder them first.

Yves.

